{"answer": "The Willow Springs Mental Health Initiative attributes its success to several core principles demonstrated across its programs:\n\n- **Education and early intervention** \u2013 integrating mental health education into school curricula to teach stress management, empathy, recognition of illness, and help\u2011seeking (Evidence\u202f1).  \n- **Technology\u2011enabled access** \u2013 using apps and online platforms (e.g., \u201cMental Health Mate\u201d) for immediate support, mood tracking, resource directories, and anonymous peer connection (Evidence\u202f2).  \n- **Workplace wellness** \u2013 training managers in mental\u2011health first aid, offering mental\u2011health days, and creating relaxation spaces to improve well\u2011being, productivity, and reduce absenteeism (Evidence\u202f3).  \n- **Peer support** \u2013 facilitating shared\u2011experience groups where participants listen, learn from one another, and act as gateways to further services (Evidence\u202f4).  \n- **Community engagement and awareness** \u2013 hosting events like the \u201cMind Matters\u201d festival that combine workshops, professional talks, and personal testimonials to break stigma, foster dialogue, and combat isolation (Evidence\u202f5).\n\nTogether, these principles\u2014education, technology, workplace support, peer networks, and community\u2011driven awareness\u2014form the foundation of the initiative\u2019s effectiveness.", "event": "final_answer", "evidence_count": 5, "llm_called": true, "not_found": false, "query_id": "gjxpphdi-q1::chain_hop::node9::attempt1", "ts_monotonic": 224369.838436669, "ts_unix": 1777954304.0266926, "worker_id": "node9"}
{"answer": "According to the Willow Springs Mental Health Initiative (as described in the evidence), the core principles behind the success of mental health initiatives are:\n\n- Training managers in mental\u2011health first aid  \n- Providing employees with mental\u2011health days off  \n- Creating spaces for meditation and relaxation within the workplace  \n\nThese principles aim to foster a supportive environment that improves well\u2011being, productivity, and reduces absenteeism. No conflicting values are presented in the provided evidence.", "event": "final_answer", "evidence_count": 7, "llm_called": true, "not_found": false, "query_id": "gjxpphdi-q1::chain_hop::node9::attempt2", "ts_monotonic": 224381.715630944, "ts_unix": 1777954315.9038868, "worker_id": "node9"}
